# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
#
# ⚠️ Content-Security-Policy is REPORT-ONLY on purpose. A hard CSP that gets an origin
# wrong fails silently in production — and the way we'd find out is broken monobank
# payments or a dead Sentry/PostHog. Report-only blocks NOTHING; it only reports
# violations (visible in the browser console / devtools). Run it like this for ~a week,
# read what would have been blocked, add any missing origins, and ONLY THEN rename the
# header to `Content-Security-Policy` to enforce.
#
# Known external origins this policy accounts for:
#   - Google Fonts:  fonts.googleapis.com (CSS) + fonts.gstatic.com (font files)
#   - PostHog (EU):  eu.i.posthog.com (ingest) + eu-assets.i.posthog.com (recorder/array scripts)
#   - Sentry:        *.ingest.sentry.io / *.ingest.de.sentry.io (error ingest)
#   - API:           same-origin /api in prod, so 'self' covers it. If the API ever moves
#                    to its own origin, the report-only phase will surface it — add it then.
# monobank checkout is a top-level navigation (window.location), not a form/XHR, so it is
# not governed by connect-src/form-action and needs no entry here.
# Before enforcing, also consider adding X-Frame-Options: DENY (frame-ancestors below is
# the CSP equivalent but is not enforced while this header is Report-Only).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://eu.i.posthog.com https://eu-assets.i.posthog.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.de.sentry.io; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
